{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 34, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "זהב ורמון פעמון זהב ורמון", :translit "zahav verimon pa'amon zahav verimon", :gloss "gold and pomegranate bell gold and pomegranate"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :gematria, :a "זהב ורמון פעמון זהב ורמון", :b "המה שבעים ושנים"}], :frame {:text "The bells and pomegranates on the high priest's robe are described in Exodus 28:33–34. The number seventy-two recalls the seventy-two letters of the divine name, which the rabbinic tradition identifies as a three-letter name expanded into seventy-two triads, transmitted to the angels in Exodus 14:19–21 (Shabbat 104a). The high priest who wears these bells and pomegranates is also associated with the explicit divine name spoken on Yom Kippur inside the Holy of Holies (Yoma 71a).", :sources ["Exodus 28:33-34" "Exodus 14:19-21" "Shabbat 104a" "Yoma 71a"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :gematria, :a "זהב ורמון פעמון זהב ורמון", :a-value 878, :b "המה שבעים ושנים", :b-value 878, :lens :standard, :by :selah, :equal? true}], :book :exodus, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:19:55.861282942Z", :model "glm-5.2"}